   "text": {
    "L1": "India's climate differs because of latitude, altitude, distance from the sea and mountains.",
    "L2": "A monsoon is not just heavy rain. It is a seasonal reversal of winds.",
    "L3": "In summer, land heats faster than the sea, so low pressure forms over north-west India.",
    "L4": "Moist south-west winds from the Indian Ocean blow in and bring most of India's rain from June to September.",
    "L5": "When these winds rise over the Western Ghats or Khasi hills, they cool and drop heavy rain on the windward side.",
    "L6": "The monsoon arrives in steps from south to north, so Kerala gets it before Delhi.",
    "L7": "From October to December, the winds reverse and bring rain to the Tamil Nadu coast.",
    "L8": "Climate shapes crops, homes, clothes, food and festivals."
   },
